2. DECISIONS WE SETTLED (and why)
---------------------------------
a) Scan keeps camera + printed-text OCR. The digital-ink handwriting recognizer
   is removed permanently; it was a separate architecture nothing in lib/ used.
b) Reports ships the new mock-data screen (from Shop reports.html). The old
   bundled-sales screen is not restored.
c) OrderHistory.who is removed entirely. No customer-name field, no name prompt.
d) Offline order history is a process-lifetime in-memory repository, not a
   null-object, because OrderProvider.complete() refuses to finish an order it
   has nowhere to record -- a null-object would mean a tablet with no connection
   cannot sell anything at all.
e) RecognizedLine stays a type, holding one String text. The multi-candidate
   machinery was dead code.
f) sales_seed.json and tool/import_sales_tracker.dart are KEPT as build-time
   inputs for a future real-data reports back end.
g) The camera integration test is DEFERRED -- it needs a physical device.


